From b4e5b7566addfaa86a81b84d4f07259d1861c217 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RTSP-on-GE11 contributors <noreply@invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] ffmpeg: enable crypto protocol for AES-128 HLS (GE11-9 context)

Same one-line policy as the retained crypto integration patch. GE11-9 now
enables libdav1d immediately after gnutls; refresh context without dropping
that upstream decoder. No protocol whitelist or TLS policy is changed here.
The new pin binds this patch and its release-specific Makefile postimage.
---
diff --git a/Makefile.in b/Makefile.in
--- a/Makefile.in
+++ b/Makefile.in
@@ -359,6 +359,7 @@ FFMPEG_CONFIGURE_ARGS := \
 	--enable-libdav1d \
 	--enable-demuxers \
 	--enable-protocol=https \
+	--enable-protocol=crypto \
 	--enable-decoders \
 	--enable-encoders \
 	--enable-bsfs \
